  "challenge": "IN-001 is HIGH and its policy is categorical: an unknown SKU cannot be fulfilled and is treated as a typo or off-catalog request, with corpus precedent (INV-1003). WidgetA/WidgetB price-match reference exactly, so the defect is isolated to WidgetC; the correct disposition is to reject and have the vendor resubmit with a catalogued SKU (or after cataloguing), not to park the invoice for open-ended human confirmation. TM-002 is only LOW and described as 'worth surfacing,' not blocking, and the vendor has zero prior invoices in-store to suggest Net 30 was ever accepted—so terms reinforce rejection rather than create an independent escalate reason. The packet already supports REJECT without human involvement.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["IN-001", "TM-002", "PR-004"]
}
